/**
 * @defgroup raze_algo Algorithms
 * @brief SIMD-accelerated and auto-vectorized range algorithms in `raze::algorithm`.
 *
 * Every algorithm is a customizable function object (`options::function_with_traits`) supporting
 * iterator-sentinel and C++23 range overloads, `constexpr` evaluation, and compile-time
 * execution modifiers via `operator[]`.
 *
 * ### Algorithm Categories
 *
 * | Group | Algorithms |
 * | :--- | :--- |
 * | @ref raze_algo_batch | `for_each`, `for_each_n` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_query | `all_of`, `any_of`, `none_of`, `equal`, `mismatch`, `starts_with`, `ends_with`, `lexicographical_compare`, `lexicographical_compare_three_way` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_find | `find`, `find_if`, `find_if_not`, `find_last`, `find_last_if`, `find_last_if_not`, `find_first_of`, `adjacent_find` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_subrange | `search`, `search_n`, `find_end`, `contains`, `contains_subrange` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_count | `count`, `count_if`, `count_if_not` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_extreme | `min`, `max`, `minmax`, `min_element`, `max_element`, `minmax_element`, `clamp` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_copy | `copy`, `copy_backward`, `copy_if`, `copy_n`, `move`, `move_backward` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_fill | `fill`, `fill_n`, `generate`, `generate_n`, `generate_random` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_transform | `transform` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_replace | `replace`, `replace_if`, `replace_copy`, `replace_copy_if` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_remove | `remove`, `remove_if`, `remove_copy`, `remove_copy_if`, `unique`, `unique_copy` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_order | `is_sorted`, `is_sorted_until`, `reverse`, `reverse_copy`, `rotate`, `rotate_copy`, `shift_left`, `shift_right`, `shuffle`, `sample`, `is_permutation`, `next_permutation`, `prev_permutation` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_partition | `is_partitioned`, `partition`, `partition_copy`, `partition_point`, `stable_partition` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_sort | `sort`, `stable_sort`, `partial_sort`, `partial_sort_copy`, `nth_element` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_binary_search | `lower_bound`, `upper_bound`, `equal_range`, `binary_search` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_set | `merge`, `inplace_merge`, `includes`, `set_union`, `set_intersection`, `set_difference`, `set_symmetric_difference` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_heap | `is_heap`, `is_heap_until`, `make_heap`, `push_heap`, `pop_heap`, `sort_heap` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_fold | `fold_left`, `fold_left_first`, `fold_right`, `fold_right_last`, `fold_left_with_iter`, `fold_left_first_with_iter` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_numeric | `iota`, `accumulate`, `reduce`, `transform_reduce`, `inner_product`, `partial_sum`, `inclusive_scan`, `exclusive_scan`, `transform_inclusive_scan`, `transform_exclusive_scan`, `adjacent_difference` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_uninitialized | `construct_at`, `destroy_at`, `destroy`, `destroy_n`, `uninitialized_default_construct`, `uninitialized_default_construct_n`, `uninitialized_value_construct`, `uninitialized_value_construct_n`, `uninitialized_copy`, `uninitialized_copy_n`, `uninitialized_move`, `uninitialized_move_n`, `uninitialized_fill`, `uninitialized_fill_n` |
 * | @ref raze_algo_swap | `swap_ranges` |
 *
 * ### Shared Concepts & Execution Model
 * - @ref raze_options — compile-time decorators (`fscalar`, `fstatic`, `fautovec`, `aligned`, `unroll`, `strict_types`, `par`).
 * - @ref dynamic_dispatch — execution tiers (native, auto-vectorized, explicit SIMD, scalar) and runtime ISA dispatch.
 * - @ref vectorization_semantics — unsequenced (`unseq`) semantics, compiler auto-vectorization, and callable rules.
 * - @ref mask_semantics — low-level lane masking used in `raze::vx`.
 */

